# faicheCourse — Conall's crash course in the garden (skyeGairdin)
#
# THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE. js/game/scenes/locations/skye/courseLines.js is
# GENERATED from it and overwritten on every compile. Edit here, not there.
#
#   node tools/dialogue/course.mjs tools/dialogue/drafts/faicheCourse.dlg --check
#   node tools/dialogue/course.mjs tools/dialogue/drafts/faicheCourse.dlg
#
# The LOGIC (when each slot is said, what the player must do) is in
# faicheCourse.js. This file is only the words.
#
# ── SYMBOLS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   == NAME   a lesson. The names are the code's; don't rename them.
#   =  NAME   a slot in the lesson: a moment the code says something.
#             Plain lines under it are Conall's (or the narrator's, in a
#             *Hint slot). One line per line on screen.
#   *  TEXT   a button the player presses, ending that slot's card.
#   >  TEXT   (under a *) what the player SAYS, if longer than the button.
#             Without one, the button's own words are shown as theirs.
#   <  TEXT   (under a *) what Conall says back.
#   %  TEXT   the Irish for the line directly above. For now each one
#             repeats the English (a placeholder: not shown as Irish, not
#             voiced). Write over it when the Irish is ready.
#   @value X  (under a *) what the button means to the course:
#               on     go on (the default)
#               again  have the lesson once more
#               wait   (meet only) not ready yet: no call to the mark
#   @goto S   (under a *) Conall's reply is slot S of this lesson (a card
#             of its own, which may have buttons of its own)
#   #         a comment
#
# A slot left out, or emptied, is simply not said. A slot ending in Hint (or
# called hint) is the NARRATOR: grey plain instructions, not Conall.
#
# Slots with buttons are cards. Others are cards or captions as the logic
# decides (captions are short, over the action).

@out js/game/scenes/locations/skye/courseLines.js


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== meet
# He is waiting in the ráth; this card opens when you come in sight.

= intro
Óró! Thou art upon thy feet again.
% Óró! Tá tú ar do chosa arís.
Art thou ready?
% An bhfuil tú ullamh?
* I am.
% Tá mé.
< Good.
% Go maith.
@value wait

# a caption, as he calls you to the marked stone
= stand
Now. Stand here.
% Anois. Seas anseo.


# a card, once you are on it
= stance
Stand thus, neither too wide, nor too narrow.
% Seas mar seo, ní ró-leathan, is ní ró-chúng.
Stand not on thy heels, nor on thy toes.
% Ná seas ar do shále, ná ar do bharraicíní.

Stand upon the ground, if you get me.
%Seas ar an tallamh, a dtuigeann tú.

All else is built upon it.
% Sin an bunchloch

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== drag
# He draws a line on the ground and walks it; then you draw yours, twice.

= intro
Now. The movement.
% Anois. An ghluaiseact.


# as he walks the line
= following
See it?
% An bhfeiceann tú?

= you
Now thy turn. 
% Tusa anois. 


# after the first line you draw
= good
Again.
% Arís.

= after
Good enough
% Sásúil


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== space
# Bare-handed. He lunges at the tile you stand on (it reddens): step off.
# Then you shove him until he goes down on one knee.

= intro

Move. But do not flee.
% Gluais. Ach ná teith.
Find space between us.
% Aimsigh spás eadrainn.

# each time you get clear (one picked in turn)
= good
Again.
% Arís.

= mid
There.
% Sin é.


Now press me, until I am brought to my knee.
% Anois brúigh orm, go dtí go mbeidh mé ar mo ghlúin.

= shoveGo
Come, then. Knock me down.
% Ar aghaidh, mar sin. Leag mé.

# each shove that lands, before the last
= shoved
Again.
% Arís.

= after
There it is. Thou hast done it, and no blade yet drawn between us.
% Sin agat é. D'éirigh leat, gan aon chlaíomh tarraingthe eádrainn fós.
Poor footing, half the battle.
% Droch-sheasamh, leath an chatha.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== sword
# You on the mark, he two tiles to your left. He throws you a practice sword.

# a caption, then the throw
= intro
Now.
% Anois.

# a card, once you've caught it
= caught
= draw
Draw now.
% Tarraing anois.

Too much wrist. Too much shoulder. Art thou pulling a net from the sea?
% An iomarca ón caol. An iomarca ón gualainn. An ag tarraingt líon ón bhfarraige atá tú?

Thy feet! Where are thy feet?
% Do chosa! Cá bhfuil do chosa?


Stand with esteem. 
% Seas le gean. 

Once drawn, the blade does not sheathe itself from fear.
% Nuair a tharraingítear í, ní théann an lann ar ais ina truaill le heagla.


#

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== calls
# The salute. A card, then: draw, salute, again, again, again. No buttons:
# the blade stays out and the fatigue lesson follows straight on.

= intro

Now we salute
% Anois, beannaímid

Salute not to thine enemy\'s honour.
% Ní chuig honóir do namhaid a bheannaíonn tú.

A salute is a word spoken inward, to thyself alone.
% Is é an beannú focal a labhraítear isteach i do chroí féin amháin.

I enter with clear mind and clean intent.
% Ar aghaidh liom le aigne ghlan is le intinn soléir.
Whatever blood I spill here, I do so with open eyes.
% Cibé fuil a dhoirtim anseo, deanaim sin le shúile oscailte.
 the first call
= salute
Salute.
% Beannaigh.


# each call after the first (four salutes in all: faicheCourse.js SALUTES)
= again
Again.
% Arís.

= enough
It will do.
% Déanfaidh sé an gnó.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== fatigue
# Strike until you're winded. "Stop." Then what you learned.

# captions: the blade stays out
= intro
Come at me, then.
% Tar orm, mar sin.
Strike, strike, strike again.
% Buail, buail, buail arís.

= stop
Stop.
% Stad.

= after
What hast thou taught thyself this hour?
% Cén ceacht a mhúin tú duit féin san uair seo?
* That I tire.
% Go dtagann an tuirse orm.
@goto core
* That every blow costs.
% Go bhfuil costas ar gach buille.
@goto core
* I do not know.
% Níl fhios agam.
@goto core

= core
This is the heart of it.
% Sin é croí na ceiste.
Strength is not the gift we seek.
% Ní hí an neart an bua a lorgaimid.
We seek the stillness behind the eyes.
% Lorgaimid an t-suaimhneas atá taobh thiar de na súile.
The great sin of the Gaelic blade is not cowardice. It is waste.
% Ní hé an t-eagala an peaca ar claíomh na nGael. Is é an cur amú é.
Better strike once and truly, rather than ten times in hope.
% Is fearr buille amháin cruinn a bhualadh ná deich mbuille le dóchas.
* I am ready.
% Tá mé réidh.
* Once more.
% Arís amháin.
@value again


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== strong
# A strong blow (hold the moon). The first is corrected; the second goes on.


# a card, after the first strong blow
= notThus
Nay, not thus.
% Ní mar sin, ní hea.
Not with the arm locked tight as a gate-bar.
% Ní leis an ngéag glasáilte chomh daingean le barra geata.
Loose thy wrist.
% Scaoil chaol do láimhe. 

# (no `after` slot: it runs on into the dummy. Add one, with buttons, and it will be used.)


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== dummy
# He stands in for the training dummy, turns everything aside, and knows
# what would have landed.

= intro
Thy wrist. Loosen it. The blade must speak
% Chaol do láimhe. Scaoil é. Caithfidh an lann labhairt ar do shon

and no tongue speaks well 
% is ní labhrann aon teanga go maith 

through a clenched jaw.
% tríd giall fásctha.



Loose it as thou wouldst loose a hound from leash.
% Scaoil é mar a scaoilfeá cú ó iall.

# captions, over the play: the first blow that would have landed
= landed
Thus. Dost thou see?
% Mar seo. An bhfeiceann tú?

= after
Thy feet betray thee.
% Feallann do chosa ort.
Look. Rooted as an oak. No. No.
% Féach. Fastaithe mar dhair. Ní hea. Ní hea.
Move thus. And thus.
% Bog mar seo. Agus mar seo.
* I am ready.
% Tá mé réidh.
* Once more.
% Arís amháin.
@value again


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== feet
# Cut him while walking a drawn line past him: three passes. He counts.

= intro
Tell me this, What use is a fine blade to a standing stone?
% Cén mhaith lann bhreá do chloch sheasaimh?

Move, and move again.
% Gluais, agus gluais arís.

Step left when their eye says right.
% Céim ar chlé nuair a deir a súil ar dheis.

Step back when their shoulders say forward.
% Céim ar gcúl nuair a deir a nguaillí ar aghaidh.

Great the fool who stands to trade blow for blow with the foe of equal iron.
% Mór an amadán a sheasann buille ar bhuille i gcoinne naimhead an comh-iarainn.

Woe to him who remains where the sword expects to find him.
% Is mairg an té ag feiteamh áit a bhfuil an lann ag súil leis.

= go
Come at me.
% Tar chugam.

# the first and second passes (the third opens the card below)
= count
One.
% A haon.
Two.
% A dó.

= after
Three.
% A trí.
Dost thou see? I have not retreated from thee.
% An bhfeiceann tú? Níor chúlaigh mé uait.
A man who steps backward loses ground he may never recover.
% An ti a thógas céim ar gcúl, cailleann sé talamh nach ngabhfaidh sé ar ais go deo b'fhéidir.
Step to the side. Step to the inside of his blade-arm, and thou art safe while he swings at empty air.
% Tóg céim ar leataobh. Tóg céim chuig taobh istigh dá ghéag claoímh, is tá tú slán fad a bhíonn seisean ag luascadh i gcoinne an taer fholamh.
* I am ready.
% Tá mé réidh.
* Once more.
% Arís amháin.
@value again


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== duel
# A real bout, three rounds, gently. Lose and you mend and go again.

= intro
Now. Thy footwork. Once more.
% Anois. Do shaothar coise. Arís amháin.
Heel first. Wrist loose. Step to the inside.
% An tsáil ar dtús. An caol láimhe scaoilte. Tóg céim ar an taobh istigh.
Again. From the beginning.
% Arís. Ón tús.

= go
Come at me.
% Tar chugam.


# when he turns your blow aside (twice at most)
= read
Thy foot is telling me where you are going.
% Tá do chos ag insint dom cá bhfuil do thríal.


= after
Thou hast the making of it.
% Tá an t-ábhar ionat.
Enough.
% Is leoir sin.
* Thank you.
% Go raibh maith agat.
* Again.
% Arís.
@value again


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== end
# The course is done: the green is open. (Narrator until Conall has words for it.)



# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
== generic

# when you press "Once more"
= again
Again.
% Arís.

